    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d72">

                <pb facs="0253" n="81" sameAs="frus:frus1917Supp01v01/pg81"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72/3117</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Turkey</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Elkus</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Constantinople</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-01-08T18:00:00+02:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">January 8, 1917, 6 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received January 10, 8 a.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2393. Newbold<anchor n="1" xml:id="d72-f1"/> has been informed by the
                    Constantinople military attaché of a neutral power that some German officers
                    just arrived from Berlin have stated to him that Germany is preparing for a <pb
                        facs="0254" n="82" xml:id="pg82"/> pitiless submarine warfare by the end of
                    February next. The Germans will, it is stated, effectively blockade by their
                    submarines the whole of the British coast and will sink without warning every
                    vessel that goes to or from England. This the Germans state will be a breach of
                    all their promises to such an extent that it will certainly bring about a
                    rupture of diplomatic relations between the United States and Germany, if not
                    war.</p>
                <p>I submit the above to the Department for what it may be worth. It may be that
                    this has been purposely reported to our Embassy in order that it should be
                    transmitted to the Department so as to induce the latter to use all its
                    influence to bring about peace.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Elkus</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
